# Verification Gate

An iteration is not "done" until the project's quality checks pass. This is
enforced two ways and you are responsible for both.

## What to run

The checks for this project are declared in `.cursor/verify.json`
(typecheck / lint / test / build). They are the single source of truth.

- Run them with the `/verify` command, or run each enabled `command` directly in
  the terminal (use this when a runtime like `node` isn't on PATH).
- If `.cursor/verify.json` has no enabled checks yet, configure it for the
  current stack (this is part of `/bootstrap`).

## Your obligation before ending a turn

1. If you changed code, run the checks.
2. If any check fails, fix the **root cause** — do not weaken, skip, or delete a
   test to make it pass, and do not claim success.
3. Only state a task is complete when checks pass (or explain precisely why a
   failure is pre-existing and unrelated to your change).

## Automated backstop

The `stop` hook (`.cursor/hooks/verify.mjs`) re-runs the checks when the working
tree is dirty and, on failure, sends you a follow-up to fix them. Treat that
follow-up as mandatory, not optional. Escape hatch for a genuinely unrelated
failure: create `.cursor/skip-verify` and explain why.
